			"id": "agent-analysis-uiability-backup-restore-state-recovery",
			"interpretation": "Independently buildable HarmonyOS Stage-model sample (one 'entry' module in build-profile.json5) demonstrating UIAbility backup-and-restore after abnormal exit. Responsibility: keep EntryAbility, EntryBackupAbility, the Index page, module wiring, resources, and tests coherent as one snippet. Boundary: all runtime code is three .ets files under entry/src/main/ets; the 7-day retention, 200KB Want cap, and no-reboot-restore claims live only in README_zh.md. Relations: EntryAbility imports @kit.AbilityKit, @kit.ArkUI, @kit.PerformanceAnalysisKit; EntryBackupAbility imports @kit.CoreFileKit; module.json5 sets mainElement EntryAbility, binds srcEntry, and registers a backup extensionAbilities entry at $profile:backup_config; tests import @ohos/hypium and @kit.TestKit. Behavior contract: onCreate calls setRestoreEnabled(true) in try/catch and reads want.parameters['myData'] into an unused local; onSaveState writes wantParam['myData']='my1234567' and returns ALL_AGREE; backup_config.json sets allowToBackupRestore:true; Index toggles its text on click. Keep srcEntry/mainElement names, the backup flag, and the [Start]/[End]/[StartExclude] doc-snippet markers consistent when refactoring.",
			"kind": "analysis",
			"limitations": ["The end-to-end restore path is not proved in code: the value read from want.parameters['myData'] in onCreate is stored in an unused local, and Index.ets contains no logic to rebuild the page stack or message from restored data, so the README's claim that page stack and onSaveState data are recovered is not demonstrated by this checkout.","No build, deploy, or device execution was performed: the README's stated constraints (RK3568 only, API 20 SDK per README versus targetSdkVersion 6.0.2(22) in build-profile.json5, DevEco Studio 6.0.0+ required) are unverified doc statements.","Retention claims in README_zh.md (7-day backup storage, 200KB Want serialization limit, no restore across device reboot) are platform behaviors asserted by documentation only; nothing in the checked-in files proves them for this sample.","The ohosTest Ability.test.ets only asserts that EntryAbility launches and reaches top; it does not exercise setRestoreEnabled, onSaveState, or any kill-and-relaunch restore scenario."],
